<h2>2. COMPLETE 240-SECOND SPOKEN PRESENTATION SCRIPT</h2>

<h3><span class='badge badge-who'>SECTION 1: WHO</span> (0:00 – 0:25 | 25 Seconds | 48 Words)</h3>
<div class='spoken-script'>
  When human beings journey to Mars, Earth will become a distant speck of light <span class='direction'>[pause - 1s]</span>—and a medical emergency call will take twenty-two minutes just to reach Houston.<br><br>
  We are <strong>Team Zero</strong>, passionate software engineers and space medicine researchers inspired by NASA’s bold vision for deep space exploration.
</div>

<h3><span class='badge badge-why'>SECTION 2: WHY</span> (0:25 – 1:05 | 40 Seconds | 78 Words)</h3>
<div class='spoken-script'>
  In microgravity, human biology undergoes profound disruption.<br><br>
  Fluids shift toward the head, triggering Spaceflight Associated Neuro-ocular Syndrome <span class='direction'>[SANS]</span>. Cosmic radiation bombards cellular DNA, while bone mineral density decays at over one percent per month.<br><br>
  NASA has invested decades into understanding these hazards through the Human Research Program.<br><br>
  Because on a three-year voyage to Mars, we cannot transport a hospital—astronauts require autonomous, scientifically validated health intelligence that operates completely independently of Earth.
</div>

<h3><span class='badge badge-what'>SECTION 3: WHAT</span> (1:05 – 1:55 | 50 Seconds | 98 Words)</h3>
<div class='spoken-script'>
  Our solution is <strong>AstraVital AI</strong>: an autonomous health monitoring and physiological digital twin platform.<br><br>
  Unlike conventional trackers that treat telemetry in isolation, AstraVital AI is anchored directly in authentic NASA research.<br><br>
  We integrate the <strong>NASA Open Science Data Repository (OSDR)</strong> and <strong>GeneLab</strong>—incorporating landmark datasets like the NASA Twins Study—paired with peer-reviewed clinical guidelines from the <strong>NASA Technical Reports Server (NTRS)</strong>.<br><br>
  Furthermore, we establish strict scientific provenance: clearly distinguishing authentic NASA research datasets, simulated real-time telemetry, and derived algorithmic analytics.
</div>

<h3><span class='badge badge-how'>SECTION 4: HOW</span> (1:55 – 3:20 | 85 Seconds | 170 Words)</h3>
<div class='spoken-script'>
  Here is AstraVital AI in action.<br><br>
  On our <strong>Mission Dashboard</strong>, ten core physiological parameters stream in real-time, prominently marked as simulated telemetry. We can configure mission seeds, trigger simulated solar flare warnings, or monitor active exercise countermeasures.<br><br>
  When a flight surgeon inspects an elevated parameter—such as heart rate or intracranial pressure—our <strong>Research-to-Dashboard connection</strong> instantly surfaces corresponding NASA OSDR studies and NTRS publications, providing full DOI citations and biological context.<br><br>
  Our dedicated <strong>NASA Research Explorer</strong> allows users to query authentic spaceflight biology datasets, while the <strong>NTRS Library</strong> categorizes clinical practice standards such as NASA-STD-3001.<br><br>
  Next, our <strong>3D Astronaut Digital Twin</strong> visualizes microgravity organ stress across the left ventricle, optic nerve, axial spine, and femur—dynamically synchronizing with telemetry.<br><br>
  Finally, our <strong>Mission Simulator</strong> projects bone resorption, cumulative cosmic radiation, and mission readiness across an entire 180 to 1,000-day interplanetary transit.
</div>

<h3><span class='badge badge-impact'>SECTION 5: IMPACT & YOUR NEEDS</span> (3:20 – 4:00 | 40 Seconds | 78 Words)</h3>
<div class='spoken-script'>
  AstraVital AI demonstrates the transformative power of NASA Open Science.<br><br>
  By unlocking decades of publicly funded research and uniting it with intelligent digital twin technology, we can support autonomous clinical decisions for the Artemis Moon bases and future crews bound for Mars.<br><br>
  Humanity is stepping into the deep space era <span class='direction'>[pause - 1s]</span>—and with AstraVital AI, our health travels with us. Thank you.
</div>

